"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. The project kicked off on June 15th with an initial phase budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The executive board has since approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing), with Omar Jensen leading the development phase that follows the design phase. Strategic partnerships with TechInnovate, a leader in AI research, have been secured to leverage their AI technology. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% increase in efficiency through proposed AI algorithms, which were discussed in a meeting on August 5th. The project is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November. Additionally, security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, will be updated effective January next year."
